<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christoph Bernhard von Galen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1606">1606</a>–<a href="/years/1678">1678</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christoph Bernhard von <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galen">Galen</a> was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Münster from 1650 to 1678. He broke the independence of the city of Münster in 1661 and built a strong standing army, earning the nickname 'Bomben-Bernd' for his use of artillery. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in 1665–1666 and again from 1672 as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christoph-bernhard-von-galen.jpg" alt="Christoph Bernhard von Galen" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Heimbach · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christoph_Bernard_von_Galen_on_Horse_by_Wolfgang_Heimbach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
